  "contentHtml": "\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <p><img src=\"https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/et-default-user.svg\" alt=\"Online Bureau\">\n                                            \n                                        </p>\n                                                                        \n                                                                                    <ul>\n                                                                                                    <li>\n                                                                                                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n                                                            \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n                                                                                                            </li>\n                                                                                                                                                    <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                                                                            </ul>\n                                                                                <ul>\n                                                                                            <li>Published On Nov 5, 2026 at 07:58 AM IST</li>\n                                                                                                                                </ul>\n                                    \n                                                                            \n                                                                        \n                                \n                                \n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>Mumbai: Apollo Hospitals has reported a 23 per cent year on year (YoY) increase in consolidated revenue to Rs 7,615 crore in the three months ending September 30, 2026.Consolidated EBITDA grew 29 per cent YoY to Rs 1,191 crore and consolidated PAT increased 32 per cent YoY to Rs 630 crore.Revenue from healthcare services increased 23 per cent YoY to Rs 3,900 crore with ebitda at Rs 937 crore.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>Hospital occupancy was at 73 per cent in Q2 FY27, compared with 69 per cent in Q2 FY26 while ARPP stood at Rs. 1,86,880 an increase of 8 per cent YoY.Revenue growth driven by volume increase in Congo Specialties and high complexity clinical work aided by key specialties like Oncology (28 per cent growth), Gastro (27 per cent), Cardiac and Ortho (20 per cent) and Urology (26 per cent).</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M -->\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>International Patient Services revenue grew 37 per cent YoY in Q2 FY27.The healthcare major said its expansion programme is on track to add approximately 5,800 beds over the next five years. Apollo’s Health and Lifestyle business reported a 20 per cent YoY growth in revenue to Rs. 429 crore.Ebitda for the business grew 20 per cent YoY to Rs 61 crore and PAT was at Rs 26 crore as compared to PAT loss of Rs 4 crore in Q2 FY26.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>Apollo HealthCo’s revenue grew by 23 per cent YoY to Rs 3,286 crore, with ebitda at Rs 193 crore and PAT at Rs. 118 crore as compared to Rs. 73 crore in Q2 FY26In the 6 months ending September, Apollo reported consolidated revenue growth of  22 per cent YoY to Rs. 14,547 crore.</p><p>Consolidated EBITDA grew 29 per cent YoY to Rs. 2,268 crore and consolidated PAT grew 33 per cent YoY to Rs. 1,211 crore.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>Dr. Prathap C. Reddy, Founder &amp; Chairman, Apollo Hospitals Group, said, “The performance in this Quarter was supported by the revenue growth driven by robust volume increase inCongo T Specialties. I am encouraged by the progress we are making across our businesses and the contribution each one of our hospitals are making to the Group.”</p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Online Bureau</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Nov 5, 2026 at 07:58 AM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Nov 5, 2026 at 07:58 AM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">2 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-subs__icon-nl\" role=\"presentation\" aria-label=\"Newsletter icon\">\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-newsletter.svg\" alt=\"Newsletter icon\" width=\"55\" height=\"55\">\n            </figure> -->\n        \n            \n                \n                    <h2>All about ETHealthworld industry right on your smartphone! </h2>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><a href=\"/app\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Download the ETHealthworld App</a> and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles.</li>\n                    </ul>\n                                            <!-- <div class=\"app-store-container desktop-view\">\n                            <a href=\"/app\" title=\"\" aria-label=\"Play Store\">\n                                <img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-g-play.png\" alt=\"\" />\n                            </a>\n                            <a href=\"/app\" title=\"App Store\">\n                                <img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" hei